{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms","id":1032931,"title":"New Arcana and Supernal Realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T14:54:07-08:00","id":1032931,"title":"New Arcana and Supernal Realms","content":"So, it is a popular theory/Headcanon/Actual Canon/Whatevs that the Supernal is much vaster than the 5 Supernal realms and there are realms beyond the 5 with the watchtowers, that the Mages can't access or don't know about beacause, well, no Watchtowers. So, drawing it a little further, there's probably also a ton of Arcana that correspond(Or not) to the stuff within the Fallen(Or other places) that we don't know about. So, what would those Arcana be? What would their realms be? Imagine someone ascends and makes a new Watchtower in one of those realms? Let's have a little thinking fun, shall we?<br /> And just beacause it's bad manners to come to own party emptyhanded, effects of brainstorming this from chat (Stemming from the idea of &quot;Let's make an Arcanum to fuck with Unchained!Demons.&quot;) (Also, for some reason, the effects are so much MtAs-y you might want to avert your eyes. I swear it wasn't intended, just sorta, came out like that.)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Realm: Tartarus<br /> Ruling Arcana:<br /> Consensus (Subtle): Affects the ways people percieve things as, amongst others. Taking some cues from Prime and Space. Baseline thought &quot;Stuff is not as people tell you it is, nor is it as you tell yourself it is, not is it as you<br /> Aether (Gross): No idea what it does beyond messing with Demons and other GM stuff. Probably taking cues from Mind and Forces. Baseline thought &quot;Stuff works beacause people think it works that way. But the stuff actually doesn't work. We just think it does.&quot;<br /> Inferior Arcanum:<br /> Stability: IDK, man, we only thought up the name.<br /> How would we call a mage from there: &quot;Illusionist of the Watchtower of the Shattered Mirror, on the Path of Vision in the realm of Tartarus, Realm of Guilt and Abode of Titans&quot;<br /> Central theme-thing: Subjectivity. You are not doing bad things unless you percieve them as bad things. You are not guilty unless you percieve yourself guilty. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Don't hurt me, we really didn't intend for it to be so Old Mage-y!<br /> So, what cool stuff do you think you can make up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:38:13-08:00","id":1032955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms#post1032931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, what would those Arcana be? [...]<br /> So, what cool stuff do you think you can make up?</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, let me say that I don't think it's non-canon to say that there are areas of the Supernal that are not governed by the five watch towers. I don't have the books with me right now, so I don't have the quotes with me right now, but reading Mage: The Awakening 2nd edition it became very clear to me that the Supernal was much vaster than the areas demarcated by the five watchtowers. <br /> <br /> That said, here we go. <br /> <br /> Here are the initial 10 arcana: Space, Time, Fate, Mind, Life, Spirit, Death, Matter, Forces, Prime. From this list, Spirit is clearly bullshit. All it does is introduce another class of ephemeral creatures and the powers to interact with them. It doesn't offer anything not already offered by Mind and Death. Secondly, from this list Death is also clearly bullshit. It governs ghosts, a separate class of ephemeral creatures that can also be governed by Goetia, and control over shadows (which should be governed by Forces, because shadows depend on light). (and, taking into account recent reports on this very forum, level-inappropriate lethal damage). It's the opposite of Life, but that does not mean it requires an arcanum of its own. Status Quo is the opposite of Forces, but it doesn't have its own arcanum.<br /> <br /> Alright, now that those bullshit arcana have been sorted out, let's turn our attention to the real issue. Looking at Time, Fate, Space, Mind, Matter, Forces, Prime, and Life, there should clearly not be an Arcanum that governs food. Going by the new classification scheme, this is an area that is controlled by both Life and Forces. The only non-alive foods used in food preparation are salt and water. Everything else was alive at some point, and so governed by Life. Forces governs the baking, mixture, separation and preparation, as well as the distribution of ingredients that was never alive. So, food is out.<br /> <br /> So what would require a new arcanum? The Abyss, obviously. For the scelesti, the Abyss even has a watchtower of its own. It's not anything like the Supernal watchtowers, because it draws its powers from the abyss, but at the same time, it kind of is. It gives a scelesti control over an area of magic, it has a database of mages who have awakened in there, it has everything a normal watchtower would have except that it is located in the Abyss. Well, what if the Abyss wasn't so bad in the long run? What if all of the effects of awakening in the Abyss were merely a PR move by the diamond orders? Perhaps the Abyss has an Arcanum of its own, governing Pacts, parts of Time, parts of Space, and parts of Mind. That's what demons do, in our non-Awakened literature. See Paradise Lost, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joost_van_den_Vondel#Lucifer_.281654.29_and_Milton.27s_Paradise_Lost\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariken_van_Nieumeghen\" target=\"_blank\">Mariken von Nimwegen.</a> So this Watchtower would govern the domain of daemons, carving out parts of the domains of several different watchtowers. I don't really see a problem there. There is no reason to suspect mind or fate are natural kinds, even looking at the philosophical literature governing natural kinds. What if the natural kind is daemonica?<br /> <br /> What else would require a new arcanum? Music. Drawing. Sculpting. All of the arts! All of them govern specific rules for achieving excellence in a medium that can not be parallelled by sophistication in the magical arts. Not even Space can govern the differences between the three, unless it's coupled with Time and Mind. So why does that mean we should take Space, Time and Mind as Primary? Why not take Music, Drawing, and Sculpting?<br /> <br /> Once you start dividing up reality into separate irreducible categories, this is the sort of problem you'll run into. Even at the bottom level, there will be various equally good systems of distribution. That's the real problem, because it will have to be solved through politics, which means it won't have a real solution.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:18:28-08:00","id":1032974,"title":"","content":"I disagree with several points but lets just choose 1. Death is so much more than just ghosts. Death has taken on the roll of Entropy, Void, and Absence. Shadow doesn't fit under forces because it ins't the control of light it is the spread of darkness, the decay and eradication of all light. If you want to look at it that way even light is a wave and has substance, therefore should fall under matter. If light didn't have substance it wouldn't be able to be blocked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:23:15-08:00","id":1032979,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm afraid I don't have anything particularly productive to bring to the table, but I'd like to point out that using your own logic regarding food, Music is governed by Forces (resonant vibrations aka kinetic energy) and Time (when the resonant vibrations occur). Similarly, Drawing is governed by Space, because it's the representation of 3 dimensional things in 2 dimensions (removing one of the 'false' distances between the objects). Sculpting is similarly governed by Matter, and you can literally become a supreme sculptor by casting Shaping at high enough potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12855-fenrir","name":"Fenrir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:22:49-08:00","id":1033024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms?p=1032955#post1032955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are the initial 10 arcana: Space, Time, Fate, Mind, Life, Spirit, Death, Matter, Forces, Prime. From this list, Spirit is clearly bullshit. All it does is introduce another class of ephemeral creatures and the powers to interact with them. It doesn't offer anything not already offered by Mind and Death. Secondly, from this list Death is also clearly bullshit. It governs ghosts, a separate class of ephemeral creatures that can also be governed by Goetia, and control over shadows (which should be governed by Forces, because shadows depend on light). (and, taking into account recent reports on this very forum, level-inappropriate lethal damage). It's the opposite of Life, but that does not mean it requires an arcanum of its own. Status Quo is the opposite of Forces, but it doesn't have its own arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some very narrow views of those Arcana.<ul><li>Spirit: Related to literal spirits, yeah, but it doesn &quot;add&quot; a new aspect to reality. Spirits exist in the Fallen World whether a Mage knows about it or not. Saying &quot;Spirit is bullshit&quot; because it allows Mages to deal with a part of reality not normally visible to others is like saying &quot;astrophysics is bullshit&quot; because it allows scientists to study and understand parts of the universe that people don't experience in their lives.</li> <li>Death: Death governs not only ghosts (which, again, exist whether Mages like it or not), but also entropy, chaos, and literal death, as well as a loss of energy (cold, darkness etc.). Ironically, this makes it the exact &quot;Status Quo&quot; Arcanum to oppose Forces. Hence Death being the Inferior Arcanum for the Force-focused Obrimoi.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what would require a new arcanum? The Abyss, obviously. For the scelesti, the Abyss even has a watchtower of its own. It's not anything like the Supernal watchtowers, because it draws its powers from the abyss, but at the same time, it kind of is. It gives a scelesti control over an area of magic, it has a database of mages who have awakened in there, it has everything a normal watchtower would have except that it is located in the Abyss. Well, what if the Abyss wasn't so bad in the long run? What if all of the effects of awakening in the Abyss were merely a PR move by the diamond orders? Perhaps the Abyss has an Arcanum of its own, governing Pacts, parts of Time, parts of Space, and parts of Mind. That's what demons do, in our non-Awakened literature. See Paradise Lost, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joost_van_den_Vondel#Lucifer_.281654.29_and_Milton.27s_Paradise_Lost\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariken_van_Nieumeghen\" target=\"_blank\">Mariken von Nimwegen.</a> So this Watchtower would govern the domain of daemons, carving out parts of the domains of several different watchtowers. I don't really see a problem there. There is no reason to suspect mind or fate are natural kinds, even looking at the philosophical literature governing natural kinds. What if the natural kind is daemonica? </div> </div> </div>...Abyssals aren't demons. The Abyss isn't the parts of Supernal symbolism that we associate with Hell and demons (that's Pandemonium). The Abyss is incoherence and falsehood, being made up of both symbols without reflection in the Fallen, and combinations of symbols that are inherently incoherent. It's the cosmic and symbolic manifestation of infectious and malignant nonsense attempting to impose itself on the order of truth and reality. I'm not saying that the Abyssal Arcanum is a bad idea <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/603390-homebrew-abyssal-arcanum\">(That would make me a hypocrite)</a>, but it can't just be &quot;a bit of Mind, a bit of Fate, a bit of Time and Space.&quot; If anything, it'd be something like an inverted Prime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms?p=1032979#post1032979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, Drawing is governed by Space, because it's the representation of 3 dimensional things in 2 dimensions (removing one of the 'false' distances between the objects).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh...The spatial relationships of the drawing are Space, but the concept a drawing represents would be Mind (or Prime, if you want to cleave to the symbolic nature of a drawing), and the medium upon which it's drawn would be Matter (or Forces if it's a digital drawing). Nearly every Arcanum can be found in some way in every thing in the Fallen World, because everything in the Fallen reflects the Supernal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:24:33-08:00","id":1033026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms?p=1032979#post1032979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm afraid I don't have anything particularly productive to bring to the table, but I'd like to point out that using your own logic regarding food, Music is governed by Forces (resonant vibrations aka kinetic energy) and Time (when the resonant vibrations occur). Similarly, Drawing is governed by Space, because it's the representation of 3 dimensional things in 2 dimensions (removing one of the 'false' distances between the objects). Sculpting is similarly governed by Matter, and you can literally become a supreme sculptor by casting Shaping at high enough potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you telling me is I should use spaces to trap my enemies in flat land? <br /> <br /> On topic I think it'd be interesting to have the abyss as its own 'true' arcana. It'd give scelesti a new depth even if the ability to use this arcana was restricted. It could even require a tutor to unlock the first dot (even if none pass it). To then be able to use the summoning system to call form beings from the abyss itself could be fascinating. However it's hard to pin down what this abyssal magic would encompass. Chaos, corruption, impossibility are a few things I can see it covering but I don't think that us clear enough for an arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:34:39-08:00","id":1033037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms?p=1033026#post1033026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you telling me is I should use spaces to trap my enemies in flat land?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously.<br /> <br /> Scelesti with the Diamond Diadem (I think I got the name right) gain the Abyss as an arcana. It's never been well defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T19:53:02-08:00","id":1033103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms?p=1033026#post1033026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what you telling me is I should use spaces to trap my enemies in flat land?<br /> <br /> On topic I think it'd be interesting to have the abyss as its own 'true' arcana. It'd give scelesti a new depth even if the ability to use this arcana was restricted. It could even require a tutor to unlock the first dot (even if none pass it). To then be able to use the summoning system to call form beings from the abyss itself could be fascinating. However it's hard to pin down what this abyssal magic would encompass. Chaos, corruption, impossibility are a few things I can see it covering but I don't think that us clear enough for an arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms?p=1033037#post1033037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obviously.<br /> <br /> Scelesti with the Diamond Diadem (I think I got the name right) gain the Abyss as an arcana. It's never been well defined.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/603390-homebrew-abyssal-arcanum\">I have something homebrewed for this.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:59:22-08:00","id":1033126,"title":"","content":"Well, the thread seems to have drifted away from &quot;new arcana&quot; and into &quot;wtf arcana&quot; pretty much immediately, so to throw in my two cents:<br /> <br /> One of the 1e-&gt;2e themes has been to make it explicit that different arcana can achieve the same effects. This does something fun, in my opinion, because you can actually broaden the scope of the various arcana in ways that make them less one-note, largely by driving a truck through the Mind Arcanum and scattering its abilities everywhere else. You already have Prime taking on the idea of truth. It was intimated during open dev that Death also covers secrets, now, and I'd like to see that more explicit than Without a Trace. Like... what does a Making spell do when you're creating a secret ex nihilo? The list of Fate domains includes &quot;intentions&quot;, but that doesn't really manifest itself in the mechanics. And then you've got Spirit which, as noted, is a bit lackluster unless you've really bought into the Shadow. During open dev, I was really hoping that it would riff off <i>zeitgeist</i> and be more explicitly heavy-handed in how you mess with spirits in order to achieve interesting effects. (Indeed, this is something that Death could use as well.) One idea I have for how to do that is by figuring out some swarm mechanics for ephemeral entities: by having a <i>lot</i> of Rank 0 or Rank 1 ghosts/spirits, you would be able to simulate a much higher-ranked entity of that kind and through it evoke some tricks. Another idea is to wrap Spirit around myth-making, and cover things like being larger-than-life, being big-spirited, having your finger on the pulse of the world, and so on.<br /> <br /> If it makes <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12787\" data-vbnamecard=\"12787\">logos</a> feel better, I'd happily throw the arts and general creativity into Spirit, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T23:50:10-08:00","id":1033188,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I like to put emotions under Spirit as well. <br /> <br /> Trying to get this back to the original topic, I don't think you're going to find anything that can't be fit into the existing ten Arcana; and my personal preference for new Paths is to play with different pairings (e.g., Fate and Space, Mind and Time, Death and Life, Prime and Matter, Spirit and Forces, etc.) instead of different Arcana.<br /> <br /> If I do go with Paths with new Arcana, my instinct is to start out on the fringes of known Supernal concepts: at the very least, the Inferior Arcanum should come from the set of known Arcana, if only because \u201cmy Inferior Arcanum is one that nobody knows anything about\u201d doesn't strike me as good game design. And I'd be inclined to use Ruling Arcana that divide the phenomena covered by the existing Arcana in a different fashion. For instance, I could maybe see a Story Arcanum (Subtle) that combines the prophetic elements of Time with the Sympathy elements of Space, or a Gross Arcanum that combines Space's facility with warping space with Time's facility with messing with the flow of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:02:51-08:00","id":1033216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032931-new-arcana-and-supernal-realms?p=1033188#post1033188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; I like to put emotions under Spirit as well.<br /> <br /> Trying to get this back to the original topic, I don't think you're going to find anything that can't be fit into the existing ten Arcana; and my personal preference for new Paths is to play with different pairings (e.g., Fate and Space, Mind and Time, Death and Life, Prime and Matter, Spirit and Forces, etc.) instead of different Arcana.<br /> <br /> If I do go with Paths with new Arcana, my instinct is to start out on the fringes of known Supernal concepts: at the very least, the Inferior Arcanum should come from the set of known Arcana, if only because \u201cmy Inferior Arcanum is one that nobody knows anything about\u201d doesn't strike me as good game design. And I'd be inclined to use Ruling Arcana that divide the phenomena covered by the existing Arcana in a different fashion. For instance, I could maybe see a Story Arcanum (Subtle) that combines the prophetic elements of Time with the Sympathy elements of Space, or a Gross Arcanum that combines Space's facility with warping space with Time's facility with messing with the flow of time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now new paths is something that I have thought of as well. I feel that the paths are were we should be changing things. Even if you pair the 5 subtle with each of the 5 gross Arcanum there would be 25 total paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:21:15-08:00","id":1033223,"title":"","content":"As for a New Arcanum, How about Balance. You can't heal something without harming something else, Empathic Healing. You can't create something without destroying something else. Example you can't create energy without the destruction of matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:50:39-08:00","id":1033248,"title":"","content":"Why would you need a new Arcana? 10 Arcana line up the world almost perfectly. Just combine existing Arcana into new Supernal Realms, if you want to. I did that in my pathless Chronicle, went good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:55:55-08:00","id":1033289,"title":"","content":"Apparently OP thinks the Arcana don't make sense, and decided to make more nonsensical arcana in response. *Shrug.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:09:34-08:00","id":1033295,"title":"","content":"Umm, no. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11117_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11117\" data-vbnamecard=\"11117\">Inquisitor</a> was putting forward a fun thought experiment, exploring some possibilities of what could be in the Supernal beyond the known Arcana. He said nothing negative about the known Arcana. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12787\" data-vbnamecard=\"12787\">logos</a> leapt into the criticism of the Arcana immediately thereafter; but he's not the OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://ti